## Lore

The pygmy shaman stands where a medicine man would in other African peoples: the typical pygmy tribe has a king, a queen, a council of elders and a shaman rather than a medicine man. He resembles both the medicine man and the druid, but he uses his magic very differently. He cannot cast spells at all; instead he pours his own P.P.E., and energy drawn from ley lines, nexuses or sacrifice, into charms and talismans that simulate spells.

His good medicine is protective and helpful. He lends his multiple-use items to whoever is in need and takes them back when the trouble has passed, and he is paid with food, drink, jewelry and a place in any home for as long as he wants it. The king and important tribe members may carry as many as four of his items; hunters one or two, for climbing, repelling animals or shadow melding; the average tribe member none.

## Talismans and Charms

Talismans (one spell each, at fourth level strength). Cost is the spell''s P.P.E. plus 40 for a single use, or plus 200 for an item usable twice per 24 hours. * = typically reserved for the shaman.

| Talisman | Spell P.P.E. | Single use | Twice per 24 hours |
|---|---|---|---|
| Chameleon | 6 | 46 | 206 |
| Climb | 3 | 43 | 203 |
| Detect Concealment | 6 | 46 | 206 |
| *Escape | 8 | 48 | 208 |
| Eyes of the Wolf | 25 | 65 | 225 |
| Float in Air | 5 | 45 | 205 |
| Heal Wounds | 10 | 50 | 210 |
| Ignite Fire | 6 | 46 | 206 |
| *Locate | 30 | 70 | 230 |
| *Negate Magic | 30 | 70 | 230 |
| Negate Poison | 5 | 45 | 205 |
| Remove Curse | 140 | 180 | 340 |
| Repel Animals | 7 | 47 | 207 |
| See the Invisible | 4 | 44 | 204 |
| *Shadow Meld | 10 | 50 | 210 |
| Swim as a Fish | 6 | 46 | 206 |
| *Time Hole | 210 | 250 | 410 |
| Tongues | 12 | 52 | 212 |
| Turn Dead | 6 | 46 | 206 |
| *Water to Wine | 40 | 80 | 240 |
| *Words of Truth | 15 | 55 | 215 |

Charms stay active for years until the shaman deactivates them or they are destroyed. Cost is the spell''s P.P.E. plus 100.

| Charm | Spell P.P.E. | Cost | Effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| Amulet (any) | half the usual | not stated | as the amulet |
| Impervious to Fire | 5 | 105 | as the spell |
| Impervious to Energy | 20 | 120 | as the spell |
| Impervious to Poison | 5 | 105 | as the spell |
| Remove Curse | 140 | 240 | +5 to save vs all of the witch''s curses |
| Stone to Flesh | 3 | 103 | impervious to petrification |
| Sickness | 50 | 150 | +2 to save vs all sicknesses |
| Metamorphosis: Superior | 100 | 200 | cannot be magically transformed against his will |
| Protection Circle: Simple | 45 | 145 | +2 save vs magic or psionic attacks, +3 vs witchcraft |
| Purification | not printed | not printed | food and water in the container cannot spoil |
| Shrink | 30 | 130 | shrinks a tall wearer to four feet until 1D4 melee rounds after removal |

## GM Notes

Most pygmy priests are Millennium druids and most pygmy medicine men are herbalists (Rifts England). The shaman''s items take a 1D4 hour creation ritual to make or recharge, so a shaman caught away from a ley line or nexus is limited by his own P.P.E.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pygmy-shaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pygmy-shaman';

